---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, toolkitReady } from '../../data/site';
---
<Base
  title={`${site.toolkitName}: Excel Workbook | Ohmetry`}
  description="An Excel workbook from the author of Ohmetry for engineers who want electrical calculations in a spreadsheet they can keep, check and adapt."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Toolkit', href: '/toolkit/' }]}
  noindex={!toolkitReady}
>
  <h1>{site.toolkitName}</h1>
  <p>The calculators on this site run in your browser and give you one answer at a time. The toolkit is a workbook you keep: the same kind of calculations in a spreadsheet you can open offline, check cell by cell and adapt to your own projects.</p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>Electrical, solar and protection engineers who check designs in Excel, and who want to see the formula behind every number. It is written by a protection engineer with MV/HV experience under IEC and Saudi practice, and the formulas are the ones explained in the guides on this site.</p>

  <h2>Why a workbook</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>You can read every formula.</strong> Nothing is hidden behind a button.</li>
    <li><strong>It works offline</strong>, on a site visit or in a plant with no connection.</li>
    <li><strong>You can change it.</strong> Add your company's factors, your cable tables and your standard sizes.</li>
    <li><strong>You can print it</strong> and attach it to a submittal.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Using it with the site</h2>
  <p>The free calculators stay free. If you only need a quick answer, use them. The workbook is for repeated checks, offline work and adapting the method. Start with the guides on <a href="/voltage-drop-formula/">voltage drop</a> and the <a href="/relay-setting-checklist/">relay setting checklist</a> to see how the calculations are explained.</p>

  {toolkitReady ? (
    <>
      <h2>Get the toolkit</h2>
      <p><a class="button" href={site.gumroadUrl}>Get the toolkit on Gumroad</a></p>

      <h2>Not ready to buy?</h2>
      <p>Leave your email and get new calculators and corrections as they are published. No spam, and you can unsubscribe at any time.</p>
      <form class="optin" method="post" action={site.emailFormAction}>
        <label>Email address
          <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
        </label>
        <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
      </form>
      <p class="meta">See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what is collected and how it is used.</p>
    </>
  ) : (
    <p class="meta">This page is a draft: the product link and email form have not been configured yet (see <code>src/data/site.ts</code>). It is hidden from search engines until they are.</p>
  )}
</Base>

<style>
  .button, .optin button { display:inline-block; font:inherit; padding:10px 18px; border-radius:6px; border:0; background:var(--accent); color:#fff; text-decoration:none; cursor:pointer }
  .optin { display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-end; flex-wrap:wrap }
  .optin label { flex:1 1 240px }
  code { background:var(--card); padding:1px 5px; border-radius:4px }
</style>
